        {
          "caption": "Comparing with == compares arrows, and these lead to two different objects: false, even though the text matches. That is error 1.",
          "print": "== comparison: false\n",
          "vars": [{"name": "input", "ref": "N"}],
          "arrays": [{"id": "P", "text": "YES", "pool": true}, {"id": "N", "text": "YES"}],
          "compare": [{"a": {"array": "P"}, "b": {"array": "N"}, "same": false}]
        },
        {
          "caption": "equals compares the characters instead: Y, E and S all match, so true.",
          "print": "equals() comparison: true\n",
          "vars": [{"name": "input", "ref": "N"}],
          "arrays": [
            {"id": "P", "text": "YES", "pool": true, "match": [0, 1, 2]},
            {"id": "N", "text": "YES", "match": [0, 1, 2]}
          ],
          "compare": [
            {"a": {"array": "P", "index": 0}, "b": {"array": "N", "index": 0}, "same": true},
